tags: $:/tags/Stylesheet
title: $:/lithic/streams-menu-fix
type: text/css

/* Adapt menu text to the contrast core's menu ink. This used to hard-bind the
   palette foreground, which defeated the contrast roles below it (an !important
   declaration cannot be outbid by specificity) and left the hover band's ink
   unreadable on mid-luminance primaries. Retyped to text/css because the
   wikitext parser rewrites a literal double hyphen into an en-dash, which would
   silently kill these var() lookups. */
.sq-contextmenu .tc-menu-list-item, .sq-contextmenu .tc-menu-list-item a {
    color: var(--lithic-c-menu-fg) !important;
    fill: var(--lithic-c-menu-fg) !important;
}

/* The Notebook theme applies `animation: pop` (which uses transform: scale) to .tc-drop-down.
   An active CSS transform creates a new stacking context, trapping the popup below the sidebar
   even with a high z-index on the outer tc-popup wrapper. The fix is to set z-index directly
   on the animated element (.sq-contextmenu is also .tc-drop-down) so it wins within its
   own stacking context relative to the fixed sidebar. */
.sq-contextmenu {
    z-index: 100000 !important;
}

/* Belt-and-suspenders: also raise the outer tc-popup wrapper */
.tc-popup:has(.sq-contextmenu) {
    z-index: 100000 !important;
}